ion transport across VM models\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:768:Second, until that format exists, cross-host transport of a parked\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:962:payload plus engine transport keys. No restore closure, stream handle,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1130:H, its scalar bytes, its validator, or its wire protocol. It does not add\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1194:- Register continuation lifting and cross-model park/resume transport.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1234:> Earlier decomposition/fold provenance remains: engine method/binding live in\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1243:- [yin.vm.linker.md](./yin.vm.linker.md): admission, offset tables, and module transport.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1244:- [yin.vm.engine.md](./yin.vm.engine.md): scheduler, effects, custody, and (`§E.1–§E.5`) the in-instance engine and dao.stream wasm binding, and K0/W0 differential conformance method.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1313:### 10.2 Sparse continuation materialization, `register-restore`, and layout transport\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1360:#### 10.2.3 Cross-runtime continuation transport and layout compatibility\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1370:If a future authorized transport carries register continuation coordinates\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1376:gate the native transport API to a verified matching layout/prefix or return\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1377:qualified `:continuation-format`; this transport restriction does not change\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1413:lowering validates binding/format, attached origin, and arity against actual\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1450:fixtures, bindings, and compared fields are listed here):\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1451:- `test/yin/vm/semantic/corpus.cljc` **programs and literal goldens**: these goldens specify syntax/address, not a runnable environment or expected final value for every entry. Supply deterministic `f`/`g`/`h`/`k`/`x`/`y`/`c`/`loop` bindings, stream fixtures, and genuine parked targets for resume cases; otherwise compare the same qualified refusal.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1458:compilability and dao.stream binding probes live in\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1474:diagnostics. Establish matching-layout register payload transport and qualified\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1529:`:non-canonicalizable` refusals rather than claiming transport support from\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1532:hash or hashing binding bytes. Add `:return-result` fixtures with empty and\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1540:Required runtime gate: Node + Wasmtime full scheduler/event/stream-binding traces using\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1541:independent scripted transports; in-instance scheduler, custody, collection and\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1579:W3 repeats W0 binding probes against real effects: full-before-append, response\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1582:unknown-acceptance transport error. Full writer wake converts once to the FFI\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1590:in-instance admission, module stores and resource/closure transport. Prepare\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1591:the Wasmer binding; its complete suite is required by W5.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1594:adapter, closure/resource transport, `store-of` restoration, `reset`/`load-image`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1630:the dao.stream binding/profile and internal linkage versioning and deterministic binary generation. Run\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1634:register image except documented resource limits or preexisting transport\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1697:1. **Native continuation transport has a limited scope.** The sources support same-model register payloads and qualified transport refusal, while the module encoder currently refuses continuations. Keep this distinction visible in API docs/tests. A full portable continuation design would require separate authorization and compatibility work, not an ad hoc wasm-only decoder.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1698:2. **Absolute `pc` layout compatibility.** The register kernel's format check tests image membership, not complete receiving-layout equivalence. That suffices for grow-only same-task use; it is not proof that arbitrary imported absolute pcs mean the same thing. The transport adapter must enforce matching layout/prefix or use a separately specified rebaser (§10.2.3). Preserve legacy restore diagnostics without presenting the legacy check as stronger than it is.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:1710:ruling. Remaining W0 feasibility/binding/ordering gates do not change the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '74,108p' docs/design/datom.world.md; sed -n '545,590p' docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md; sed -n '622,646p' docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md; tail -5 docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '74,108p' docs/design/datom.world.md; sed -n '545,590p' docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md; sed -n '622,646p' docs/design/yin.vm.engine.md; tail -5 docs/design/yin.vm.rust-kernel.md\"","aggregated_output":"**The system ABI.** `dao.stream` is the one ABI of datom.world and `yin.vm`,\nthe only contract crossing a trust domain. Nodes interoperate through canonical\nstream values (Jing CBOR and content identities), exhaustive stream outcome maps,\nand append/park/resume. A ws or UDP transport, or wasm imported functions over\nlinear memory, is a **binding of this ABI**, never a second semantic contract.\nThe wasm binding is specified once in [yin.vm.engine.md](./yin.vm.engine.md) §E.3.\n\nWhat crosses a trust domain is a strict subset of in-machine values: closures\nand continuations cross only as admissible portable plain data; host types,\nresources and code artifacts never do. The custody gates retain this distinction\n([yin.vm.linker.md](./yin.vm.linker.md)); a physical binding grants no additional\nportability or authority.\n\n**Owner ruling, strengthened 2026-10-19: the boundary is drawn, not found;\none ABI is the principle.** The boundary between wasm and datom.world is\n`dao.stream`; its implementation uses whatever wasm exposes to the outside\nworld. The exposed functions are **adapters to dao.stream**, which is the ABI\nto `yin.vm` and the whole ecosystem. Machine-internal work executes inside the\nwasm instance: the Rust engine crates and compiled register bodies share memory\nand direct calls. Only effects/facts cross through the stream adapters. World\nfacts still require interaction with the world; moving engine implementation\ninside the machine does not manufacture those facts.\n\n**Dated supersession (owner boundary clarification, 2026-10-19):** This replaces\nthe earlier same-day “sole justification … performance” allowance for a second\nprocess-local ABI and the service-protocol interpretation of\n`yin.vm.engine.host.v1` (historically renamed from `yin.register.host.v1`). There\nis no second ABI to justify. Its private operation vocabulary, TLV codec,\nexpanded-canonical-bytes comparator and service-status protocol are dissolved.\nPerformance work optimizes internal execution or the stream binding; it does\nnot reintroduce a semantic service interface. [yang.wasm.md](./yang.wasm.md)\nis the compiler implementation plan for this in-instance architecture.\n\n**Effects out.** Portable code appends an effect value describing what must\nhappen. A host interpreter consumes that stream, performs the operation, and\n### E.3 The dao.stream wasm binding\n\n**Owner supersession, 2026-10-19 (boundary clarification):** the former\n`yin.vm.engine.host.v1` service protocol (previous name `yin.register.host.v1`)\nis dissolved, including control-block tables, operation envelopes, TLV tags,\nexpanded-canonical-bytes comparator, service statuses and NEED_SPACE/refetch.\nThe earlier performance exception is superseded. This section defines only a\nphysical binding of [dao.stream](./dao.stream.md); it adds no stream outcomes,\nsemantic operations, private codec or second ABI.\n\n#### E.3.1 Imported adapter surface\n\nUse import module `dao.stream` with the following proposed binding names.\nAll parameters and single results are i32. `p,n` address one canonical Jing\nCBOR value; `out,cap` denote a disjoint writable response region. The returned\ni32 is the **encoded response byte length**, never a status number. Decode\nthat response into the operation's exhaustive outcome map. Zero-copy views\nmust not outlive the synchronous call or memory growth.\n\n| Import | Parameters → result | Existing stream operation |\n|---|---|---|\n| `create` | `(p,n,out,cap) → length` | `create!` on a creation specification (VM make-stream adapter). |\n| `attach` | `(p,n,out,cap) → length` | `attach!` on a portable descriptor. |\n| `descriptor` | `(handle,out,cap) → length` | `descriptor`. |\n| `cursor` | `(handle,p,n,out,cap) → length` | `cursor` with decoded anchor. |\n| `next` | `(handle,p,n,out,cap) → length` | `next` with decoded cursor; the poll operation. |\n| `append` | `(handle,p,n,out,cap) → length` | `append!` with decoded value. |\n| `close` | `(handle,out,cap) → length` | `close!`. |\n\nMake/poll are VM-facing terminology, not additional stream operations. Park,\nresume, resolve-var, primitive application, state reads, roots, collection and\nmodule handling have **no imports**: they execute in-instance. Imports never\nname arbitrary FFI operations. Memory/table provision and module instantiation\nare runtime linkage/lifecycle mechanics, not semantic service operations.\n\nOperational stream handles cannot themselves be canonical data. The binding\nrepresents the handle field in a successful create/attach outcome by a checked,\ntask-local i32 slot, encoded as a Jing integer; decoding reconstructs the local\nhandle resource before the engine consumes the outcome. This is the physical\nrepresentation of an existing handle, not a guest stream identity or a portable\ncapability. Keep this binding handle namespace distinct from ValueRefs, check\nownership/lifetime, and never publish it in a stream value, continuation or\nmodule payload. Portable descriptors/cursors and all other outcome fields use\ntheir actual canonical data. Repeated reads remain non-destructive; the adapter\nhas no privileged reader and introduces no callbacks.\n\n#### E.3.3 Canonical bytes and authority\n\nRequests and outcome data use exactly Jing's canonical CBOR (§E.2.2), with its\nown ordering, numeric carriers, validation and decode/re-encode rules. Length\nparameters delimit one CBOR value; no TLV or alternate framing wraps it.\nCanonical maps/sets use repository ordering, never task handles or arena ids.\nRegister image checksums still use the register codec. Buffer access grants no\npermission to pass internal Values, private engine snapshots or trusted wrappers\nacross custody gates. Stream history records effects/facts, not register loads,\nroot materialization or other machine-internal traffic.\n\n### E.4 Composition adapters and the single in-instance engine\n\n#### E.4.1 Execution and embedding responsibilities\n\nNode/browser, Wasmtime and Wasmer provide the same stream binding (§E.3).\nThe composition hosts adapters and their actual transports/bridge interpreters;\nit does not implement resolve-var, primitives, stores, GC, continuations or the\nscheduler for wasm. A WASI-based composition may implement transports below the\nbinding; the VM core imports no WASI. There is no JS dependency in native runs.\nThe CLJS engine is the reference oracle, not a second production wasm engine.\n\nThe in-instance engine owns run-loop/scheduler-round, step budgets, ready/wait\nqueues and terminal checks. A step performs exactly one guest instruction; run\nkeeps the original ready-queue/terminal ordering and returns on the same blocked,\nRelated specs: [yin.vm.engine.md](./yin.vm.engine.md) (§E.1–§E.5, in-instance engine, dao.stream wasm binding, and K0/W0 conformance method); [yang.wasm.md](./yang.wasm.md) (register-image-to-wasm lowering); [yin.vm.debruijn.register.md](./yin.vm.debruijn.register.md) (§10, register wasm execution instance, K0/W0 register fixture schema, and register W0–W6 / Rust K1–K5 lane gates).\n\n2026-10-18: Added the owner-authorized wasm-plan and shared-kit pointers; revision 2 status and all other normative content are unchanged.\n2026-10-19: Owner-directed decomposition and fold of the 2026-10-18 wasm consensus into yang.wasm.md (lowering), yin.vm.engine.md §E.1–§E.5 (guest-agnostic execution host, service protocol yin.vm.engine.host.v1, and conformance method), and yin.vm.debruijn.register.md §10 (register wasm execution instance, register fixture schema, and register W0–W6 / Rust K1–K5 lane gates), retiring yin.vm.register-wasm.md and yin.vm.conformance-kit.md; revision 2 status and line coordinates 1–1334 are unchanged.\n2026-10-19 owner boundary clarification: the wasm plan now depends on compiling the K-phase Rust crates to wasm32-unknown-unknown as its in-instance engine; the composition supplies only dao.stream adapters. This pointer supersedes the historical service-protocol wording in the line-1300 pointer and earlier footer; revision 2 design-only status, file name and coordinates 1–1334 remain unchanged.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nroot=Path('docs/design'); names=['datom.world','yin.vm.engine','yang.wasm','yin.vm.debruijn.register','yin.vm.rust-kernel']\nold={n:(root/(n+'.md')).read_text() for n in names}; new=dict(old)\ncommon=[('dao.stream wasm binding','wasm implementation of dao.stream'),('dao.stream binding','dao.stream implementation'),('stream-binding','stream-adapter'),('Stream-binding','Stream-adapter'),('stream binding','stream implementation'),('binding-reservation','adapter-reservation'),('feasibility/binding/ordering','feasibility/adapter/ordering')]\nfor n,s in new.items():\n for a,b in common:s=s.replace(a,b)\n new[n]=s\ns=new['datom.world']; a=s.index('**The system ABI.**'); b=s.index('What crosses a trust domain',a)\ns=s[:a]+'''**The system ABI.** One abstraction boundary (\"'`dao.stream`), many\nimplementations (ring-buffer, websocket, UDP, wasm imports). `dao.stream` is\nthe contract for datom.world and `yin.vm`: operations, exhaustive outcome maps,\ncanonical values, append-only batch semantics and observer discipline. It is\nnot a transport implementation or a wire protocol. The wasm import-surface\nimplementation is specified once in [yin.vm.engine.md](./yin.vm.engine.md) §E.3;\nits canonical Jing CBOR representation does not define the abstraction itself.\n\n**Owner clarification, 2026-10-19 (verbatim):** “dao.stream is an abstraction\nboundary. It is not a transport implementation. It can be implemented using a\nring-buffer, a websocket or UDP”\n\nThe wasm import surface is another implementation: adapters implement the\nabstraction through imported functions over linear memory. A co-resident\nproducer can instead use an in-memory ring-buffer implementation inside the\ninstance with zero host crossings. Both preserve the same abstraction contract.\n\n'\"'''+s[b:]\ns=s.replace('a physical binding grants','an implementation grants').replace('one ABI is the principle.**','one abstraction boundary is the principle.**').replace('the earlier same-day “sole justification … performance” allowance for a second\\\\nprocess-local ABI and the service-protocol interpretation of','the earlier same-day “sole justification … performance” allowance for\\\\nprocess-local services and the service-protocol interpretation of').replace('There\\\\nis no second ABI to justify. Its private operation vocabulary, TLV codec,','Its private operation vocabulary, TLV codec,')\nnew['datom.world']=s\ns=new['yin.vm.engine']\npairs=[('wasm stream implementation','wasm implementation of dao.stream'),('The binding never','The implementation never'),('binding-specific encoding','implementation-specific encoding'),('independent of physical stream transport','independent of the stream implementation'),('### E.3 The wasm implementation of dao.stream','### E.3 The wasm implementation of the dao.stream abstraction'),('physical binding of [dao.stream](./dao.stream.md); it adds no stream outcomes,\\\\nsemantic operations, private codec or second ABI.','wasm import-surface implementation of the [dao.stream](./dao.stream.md)\\\\nabstraction; it adds no stream outcomes, semantic operations or private codec.\\\\nThe owner’s 2026-10-19 taxonomy clarification applies here: dao.stream is the\\\\nabstraction boundary, not a transport or wire protocol; ring-buffer, websocket,\\\\nUDP and wasm import surfaces are implementations. With a co-resident producer,\\\\nan in-instance ring-buffer implementation can perform stream operations with\\\\nzero host crossings. The adapter signatures and Jing bytes below specify the\\\\nimport-surface implementation, not a requirement that every implementation\\\\nserialize or cross into the host.'),('proposed binding names','proposed import names'),('The binding\\\\nrepresents','The import-surface implementation\\\\nrepresents'),('binding handle namespace','adapter handle namespace'),('Invalid binding calls','Invalid adapter calls'),('The composition hosts adapters and their actual transports/bridge interpreters;','The composition hosts the imported adapters, their underlying stream\\\\nimplementations and bridge interpreters;'),('A WASI-based composition may implement transports below the\\\\nbinding;','A WASI-based composition may supply stream implementations through these\\\\nadapters;'),('Binding-specific probes','Adapter-specific probes'),('transport test group','adapter test group'),('binding canonicalization','adapter payload canonicalization'),('wasm32 and binding gates','wasm32 and adapter gates'),('W0 binding probes','W0 adapter probes'),('rejected binding calls','rejected adapter calls'),('proposed physical bindings','proposed imports for this implementation')]\nfor a,b in pairs:s=s.replace(a,b)\ns=s.replace('Requests and outcome data use exactly Jing', 'In the import-surface implementation, requests and outcome data use exactly Jing')\nnew['yin.vm.engine']=s\ns=new['yang.wasm']\nfor a,b in [('binding defined in','implementation specified in'),('representation/binding/conformance','representation/implementation/conformance'),('transports/FFI below the same stream implementation','stream implementations/FFI through the same adapters'),(\\\"binding's operations\\\",\\\"import-surface implementation's operations\\\"),('External bindings carry','External adapters carry'),('physical binding names','physical import names'),('New binding names','New import names')]:s=s.replace(a,b)\ns=s.replace('binding to','binding to')\ns=s.replace('Engine-in-guest is mandatory, not a W6 experiment.','Engine-in-guest is mandatory, not a W6 experiment. Owner taxonomy clarification,\\\\n2026-10-19: dao.stream is the abstraction boundary; ring-buffer, websocket, UDP\\\\nand the wasm import surface are implementations. The module imports the\\\\nimplementation specified in engine §E.3; a co-resident in-instance ring-buffer\\\\ncan satisfy stream operations without host crossings.')\nnew['yang.wasm']=s\ns=new['yin.vm.debruijn.register']\nfor a,b in [('engine method/binding','engine method/implementation'),('hashing binding bytes','hashing adapter bytes'),('W0 binding probes','W0 adapter probes'),('the Wasmer binding','the Wasmer adapter implementation')]:s=s.replace(a,b)\ns=s.replace('> deleted. Fixtures and register transition semantics survive unchanged.','> deleted. Fixtures and register transition semantics survive unchanged.\\\\n> Owner taxonomy clarification, 2026-10-19: dao.stream is an abstraction\\\\n> boundary; ring-buffer, websocket, UDP and wasm import surfaces implement it.\\\\n> Stream operations with co-resident producers may use an in-instance\\\\n> ring-buffer with zero host crossings; the import adapter contract is unchanged.')\nnew['yin.vm.debruijn.register']=s\ns=new['yin.vm.rust-kernel']; s=s.replace('revision 2 design-only status, file name and coordinates 1–1334 remain unchanged.','revision 2 design-only status, file name and coordinates 1–1334 remain unchanged. Owner taxonomy clarification, 2026-10-19: dao.stream is the abstraction boundary; ring-buffer, websocket, UDP and wasm import surfaces are implementations, including co-resident in-instance streams without host crossings.')\nnew['yin.vm.rust-kernel']=s\nassert old['yin.vm.rust-kernel'].splitlines(True)[:1334]==s.splitlines(True)[:1334]\ndef section(s,a,b):return s[s.index(a):s.index(b)]\nfor n,a,b in [('yang.wasm','| Opcode |','### 3.4'),('yin.vm.engine','| Import |','Make/poll'),('yin.vm.debruijn.register','### 10.4 ','### 10.5 ')]:assert section(old[n],a,b)==section(new[n],a,b)\nfor n,s in new.items():\n (root/(n+'.md')).write_text(s)\n print(n+':')\n # report exact replaced lines, compact distinct terms handled separately\n print('  lines changed:',len(set(old[n].splitlines())-set(s.splitlines())))\nprint('PASS: Rust prefix, import signatures, opcode rows and fixture schema unchanged')\nPY\nrg -n -i 'binding|second.*ABI|wire protocol|transport implementation' docs/design/{datom.world,yin.vm.engine,yang.wasm,yin.vm.debruijn.register,yin.vm.rust-kernel}.md\ngit diff --check\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
